<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Berthout</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Berthout family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Berthouts were a powerful noble family of the Duchy of Brabant, lords of Grimbergen and later advocates and lords of Mechelen. From the 12th to the 14th century they contested control of Mechelen with the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Liège, to whom the town nominally belonged, and with the dukes of Brabant, whose leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> they were.</p></div>
